# Era 1, The Exchange: the self-lies that arm the inner arena (Fond of Them for Abel, The Lantern for Josh), the
# era's lore and the records the deepening pass needs. Story lead, 2026-10-23. DRAFT: every line waits for the
# author's line approval (ledger row S14). The arena fights are the combat track's; this file only arms them: a
# self-lie heard in era 1 is echoed word for word in Ilo's witness (e1_witness.lwd).

@fact e1.dog_loosed
@fact e1.dog_called

@char e1.hob
name: Hob Gedge, carter
speaker: HOB
faction: millstreet
about: Forty-six. Carted for Orme twenty years at the full rate. Gedge's father.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the self-lies
@selflie e1.sl.fond
about: PRIDE, at the harvest supper, as the professor toasts the Hesh temperament (e1_board.lwd, e1.toast)
happened: The harvest supper: Ilo Haldane in the yard with his plate on his knees while the barn laughed at the toast. He had been made to come in and sing for it. ? has(e1.toast_heard)
happened: The harvest supper: the hands in the yard went quiet under the window while the barn laughed.

@selflie e1.sl.lantern
about: BALLAST, at the road post after the frost list, with the post book in his hand (e1_hill.lwd, e1.post.will)
happened: The Sallises went up the hill road at the first frost. Ketti Sallis died in the hut at the top in January, and Arn laid the wall stones over her. ? has(e1.sallis_sent)
happened: Will Brack's lip split on the post book's corner, and his nose bled on the frost in the rut. ? !has(e1.sallis_sent)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- lore
@chain e1.name
name: How Haldane was written
# one run of either class sees the slip and the ruled column at the census table
route: one-run | e1.lore.slip, e1.lore.column

@lore e1.lore.slip
chain: e1.name
layer: surface
where: node e1.census.name
about: The copy slip in Walter Mott's hand: HALDANE, I., after the farm. His sevens have no bar through them.

@lore e1.lore.column
chain: e1.name
layer: deep
where: node e1.census.bet
requires: class inspector
about: The census register, the Haldane entry: the father column ruled through with a ruler, and in pencil in the margin, per A.F., or per letter, A.F.

@chain e1.hands
name: Fit to travel
# the list on the nail, and the doctor's slips on the back of it: the militia line holds both
route: one-run | e1.lore.frost_list, e1.lore.fit_slips

@lore e1.lore.frost_list
chain: e1.hands
layer: surface
where: node e1.frost
about: The frost list on the post board in Edwin Mott's round hand: HANDS, SEASONAL, NOT RESIDENT, twenty-odd names and their households.

@lore e1.lore.fit_slips
chain: e1.hands
layer: hidden
where: node e1.post.will
requires: class militia
about: Pinned behind the frost list, a slip for every name, each signed the same: fit to travel, O. Lind. The signature on the last ones is a line.
